// Who is on the map, and where they start.
//
// An encounter is a ROSTER: one entry per unit, each naming an archetype and one
// placement. A scenario names the encounter it wants by path, the same way it names its
// world and its sky, so this file is reused by every generated map that publishes the
// two standard anchors — six of them today.
//
// FIELDS
//
//   name      what logs and setup failures call this encounter
//   rosters   one entry per side. A faction may appear more than once, which is how two
//             hostile groups hold different ground
//     faction   Player or Hostile
//     placement where this side's units come in, unless a unit names its own
//     units     the units, in the order they spawn
//       archetype  what kind of unit it is — looked up in lattices.ron — it is the name an
//                  archetype's lattice will be looked up by
//       placement  OPTIONAL Some(...) for the one unit that must be somewhere exact
//
// PLACEMENTS
//
//   Fixed((x: 0, y: 4, z: -4))   an authored coordinate; the unit takes the LOWEST
//                                surface there it fits on. Cube coordinates MUST SUM
//                                TO ZERO: x + y + z == 0.
//                                See https://www.redblobgames.com/grids/hexagons/
//   Anchor("party_start")        one exact surface published by the generator, level
//                                included. Generated maps use this: rerolling the seed
//                                moves the useful ground and the anchor moves with it
//   Formation(center: ..., spread: N)
//                                a centre plus how many WALKING STEPS from it units may
//                                be placed. The first unit stands on the centre and each
//                                one after it takes the next free surface, closest
//                                first. Steps, not hexes: a formation will not spread
//                                across a chasm, onto a ledge the body cannot climb, or
//                                under a ceiling it does not fit beneath
//
// `Fixed` and `Anchor` each hold exactly ONE unit — two units sharing one is rejected
// when this file parses, and the fix is a formation. A formation is also how a named
// spawn zone is written: the anchor names it and `spread` bounds it.
//
// Every rostered unit is placed or the game returns to the title screen saying which
// entry could not be, so a unit is never quietly missing from a fight.
//
// TO ADD A PARTY MEMBER: add a line to `units`. Nothing else changes — the formation
// finds it a surface. (The interface has not caught up yet: selection, the camera and
// the hostile AI are all still written for one piece a side, so a bigger roster is
// playable but not yet pleasant.)
(
    name: "Anchored Skirmish",
    rosters: [
        (
            faction: Player,
            // The party gathers on the anchor the generator promises is good ground.
            placement: Formation(center: Anchor("party_start"), spread: 2),
            units: [
                (archetype: "hedge-mage"),
            ],
        ),
        (
            faction: Hostile,
            placement: Formation(center: Anchor("hostile_start"), spread: 2),
            units: [
                (archetype: "raider"),
            ],
        ),
    ],
)
